vulkan: load the Vulkan loader at runtime instead of linking it

ggml-vulkan resolves every entry point through its own dispatcher; the one
link-time import, vkGetInstanceProcAddr, meant a binary built with the backend
could not start on a machine without a Vulkan loader (missing vulkan-1.dll on
Windows, libvulkan.so.1 on Linux). Open the loader with vulkan-hpp's
DynamicLoader instead; without one, ggml_vk_instance_init throws, the backend
registers no devices, and the process continues on the CPU. New CMake option
GGML_VULKAN_DYNAMIC_LOADER, default ON.

Upstream: ggml-org/ggml#1614.

